Dear geomorph-ers,

We are advertising for a new postdoc to join our Villum Synergy-funded project on Stochastic Morphometry <https://www.ccem.dk/>! This 2-year position at the University of Copenhagen, Denmark, will focus on linking genotypes to phenotypes in birds, using whole-genome data from the B10K project <https://b10k.genomics.cn/>, combined with 3D morphology from markmybird.org <https://www.markmybird.org/>, MorphoSource, and other sources.

The project will be carried out in close collaboration with a dynamic team of researchers working on the mathematics of differential geometry and shape transformation, and biologists working on computational genomics and phylogenetics (~15 group members). The position will be supervised by myself and Rasmus Nielsen, with potential research stays at UC Berkeley.

See the full advert here <https://candidate.hr-manager.net/ApplicationInit.aspx/?cid=1307&departmentId=19217&ProjectId=160326&MediaId=5&SkipAdvertisement=false> for more information, or contact me directly with any questions.

Best,
Christy

Dr Christy Anna Hipsley | Associate Professor
Department of Biology, University of Copenhagen
https://evomorpholab.com <https://www.evomorpholab.com/>
@EvoMorphoLab_KU <https://twitter.com/EvoMorphoLab_KU>

