Dear all,

I'm still stuck with phylogenetic analysis.

First, I do mean shapes using the function:

Lisso.means<-lapply(coords.subset(gdf$shape, classifier$Species), FUN = mshape)
Lisso.means1<-as.matrix(Lisso.means)

When I list out dimnames they are sorted alphabetically

dimnames(Lisso.means1)

[1] "Lissotriton_boscai"      "Lissotriton_graecus"     "Lissotriton_helveticus"  "Lissotriton_montandoni"
[5] "Lissotriton_schmidtleri" "Lissotriton_vulgaris

I need the taxa to be sorted as in the tree.

I tried function:

identical (dimnames (Lisso.means1), LissoPhy$tip.label)

which reports FALSE

Then I tried to make a new order vector:

newOrder <- match (LissoPhy$tip.label, dimnames (Lisso.means1)[[1]])

and

Lisso.means2<-Lisso.means1[newOrder, drop=FALSE]

This reorders the species means as it should, but loses dimension names despite drop=FALSE.
So there's nothing to match.

Then, I tried to name dimensions manually

Lisso.means3<-as.matrix(Lisso.means2)
my_dimensions<-list(c("Lissotriton_vulgaris", "Lissotriton_schmidtleri", "Lissotriton_graecus", "Lissotriton_montandoni", "Lissotriton_helveticus", "Lissotriton_boscai"))
dimnames(Lisso.means3)<-my_dimensions

Which works

But for the function:

identical (dimnames (Lisso.means3), LissoPhy$tip.label)

I get FALSE again despite taxa being in the same order

> LissoPhy$tip[1]
"Lissotriton_vulgaris"    "Lissotriton_schmidtleri" "Lissotriton_graecus"     "Lissotriton_montandoni"
[5] "Lissotriton_helveticus"  "Lissotriton_boscai"

> dimnames(Lisso.means3)
[[1]]
[1] "Lissotriton_vulgaris"    "Lissotriton_schmidtleri" "Lissotriton_graecus"     "Lissotriton_montandoni"
[5] "Lissotriton_helveticus"  "Lissotriton_boscai"
 [[2]]NULL

However, I noticed that I have a "NULL" dimension in my mean shape data.

I probably missed a step again.

All the best,
Aleksandar

