Hi Aleksandar,

identical() tests for exact matches, so it will say false if you compare a list to a vector that is not a list.

> identical(c("A", "B"), list("A", "B"))
[1] FALSE
> identical(c("A", "B"), c("A", "B"))
[1] TRUE

Try "identical(dimnames (Lisso.means3)[[1]], LissoPhy$tip.label)", which will take the dimnames of the first dimension. This dimension contains your species names and should be comparable to $tip.label.

Best,
Bryan

